      "content": "1. Tissue – Definition"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Tissues are groups of similar cells performing a specific function, divided into Plant Tissues and Animal Tissues.",
        "Plant tissues are classified into actively dividing Meristematic Tissues and mature Permanent Tissues.",
        "Permanent plant tissues are categorized into Simple Permanent Tissues and Complex Permanent Tissues.",
        "Animal tissues are classified into four distinct major categories: Epithelial, Connective, Muscular, and Nervous Tissue."
      ],
